# Project conventions (Cursor)

Cursor agents in this repo follow the same working notes as Claude. Read and follow
@CLAUDE.md — it is the single source of truth for project conventions; keep the two
in sync rather than duplicating content here.

Key points (see `CLAUDE.md` for full detail):

- **App**: one server-rendered PHP 8.1+/MySQL app — six modules under a single PIN
  login, no build step. Migrations are idempotent (`php migrate.php`);
  `includes/config.php` is gitignored (never commit DB credentials). Deploy is a
  cPanel git-pull driven by `.cpanel.yml`.
- **Cloud Agent dev environment**: two interchangeable setups live in `.cursor/`
  (`mysql` = committed default, `mariadb`). Cursor reads the single active
  `.cursor/environment.json`; switch with `bash .cursor/use-env.sh <mysql|mariadb>`
  and commit. Each agent is isolated (own VM/DB/config/port), so multiple people can
  run agents without collisions — but do NOT flip the committed env on shared
  branches (it changes it for everyone and causes merge conflicts). Details in
  `.cursor/README.md`.
- **MySQL in the Cursor sandbox** (encoded in `.cursor/mysql-up.sh`): start `mysqld`
  in the foreground under `nohup` (the SysV `su - mysql` path and `mysqld --daemonize`
  are unreliable in containers), and set `innodb_use_native_aio=OFF` +
  `innodb_flush_method=fsync`. Prebuilt environment builds can't validate MySQL (the
  prebuild FUSE store rejects InnoDB `close()`), so rely on just-in-time `install.sh`.

## Claude-only items that do NOT apply in Cursor

`CLAUDE.md` documents the **gstack** skill system (slash-commands like `/browse`,
`/review`, `/ship`, `/learn`). Those are Claude Code commands installed under
`~/.claude` and are NOT available in Cursor. Do not try to invoke gstack skills or
the `mcp__claude-in-chrome__*` tools here — use Cursor-native tooling instead.
